            "Cache->HDD-Schreibgeschwindigkeit: WB-Ziel ist die von bcache gemeldete bzw. gedrosselte Hintergrund-Writeback-Rate. HDD-Schreiben wird zusätzlich aus /sys/block/<Gerät>/stat berechnet und liegt näher an der physischen Schreibrate.",
            "cache_mode: writethrough/writeback/writearound/none steuert, wie bcache Lese- und Schreibzugriffe behandelt. Besonders writeback kann Dirty Data puffern.",
            "writeback_percent/running: Zielprozentsatz für Dirty Data und Status des Hintergrund-Writebacks. Wichtig, damit Dirty Data nicht dauerhaft liegen bleibt.",
            "",
            "Tasten: Q beenden | S Einstellungen | R Docker neu laden | I diese Info",
        ]
    return [
        f"Linux Bcache Monitor v{__version__}",
        "Credits: by Fabian Schmeltzer",
        "AI note: This program was written with AI assistance and may contain errors.",
        f"Bug reports: {issue_url}",
        "",
        "Legal note (not legal advice): This tool is provided without warranty. Before production use, verify license, liability, and suitability. Without an explicit open-source license, standard copyright rules generally apply; GitHub primarily allows viewing and forking public repositories within platform terms. For binding legal questions, consult legal counsel.",
        "",
        "Values on the main screen:",
        "EFF: Cache efficiency = Total Hits / (Total Hits + Total Misses). Important because low values indicate many reads hit HDD instead of SSD cache.",
        "DIRTY: Amount of data in cache that still must be written back to the backing device/HDD. Important in writeback mode due to performance and failure risk.",
        "MISS/HIT: Ratio of current misses per second to hits per second. Important because values >= 1 indicate more requests bypass cache than are served by it.",
        "LIVE HIT/s and MISS/s: Current per-second change of bcache counters. Important for load spikes and live diagnosis.",
        "GRAPH: Red line = MISS/s, green line = HIT/s. Useful for spotting short peaks and trends faster than raw numbers.",
        "H/M current/avg/peak: current value, window average, peak value. Useful to compare live values with recent history.",
        "MIX: Share of current bcache events; M is miss share, H is hit share. At 0/s total load, the tool shows MIX idle because percentages are not meaningful.",
        "DELTA: Comparison of current values with window average. During idle or very small baseline, n/a is shown because percentages like -100% would be misleading.",
        "HEALTH: Traffic-light status from EFF, MISS/HIT, and miss trend. Useful as a quick warning; it does not replace root-cause analysis.",
        "CACHE NUMBERS: Total hits/misses, efficiency, peak rates, cache mode, cache size, writeback target rate, real HDD write throughput, and available writeback share.",
        "CONTAINERS CPU/RAM/DISK: Docker statistics. DISK shows read/write rates from Docker BlockIO deltas and keeps last values until the next Docker sample.",
        "",
        "Additional info and limits:",
        "HDD/backing size: Calculated from /sys/block/<device>/size. Used/free filesystem space is discovered via /proc/self/mountinfo and /proc/mounts, including resolved /dev/disk/by-* paths.",
        "SSD/cache size: Calculated when sysfs exposes data, via bcache cache*/bucket_size * nbuckets. Available writeback share uses cache_available_percent.",
        "Cache->HDD write speed: WB target is bcache's reported/throttled background writeback rate. HDD write is additionally calculated from /sys/block/<device>/stat and is closer to physical write speed.",
        "cache_mode: writethrough/writeback/writearound/none controls how bcache handles reads/writes. In particular, writeback can buffer dirty data.",
        "writeback_percent/running: Dirty data target percentage and whether background writeback is active. Important so dirty data does not remain indefinitely.",
        "",
        "Keys: Q quit | S settings | R reload Docker | I this info",
